/**
 * @file src/AnalysisG/events/gnn/include/inference/gnn-event.h
 * @brief Header file for the gnn_event class.
 * 
 * Defines the gnn_event class, which inherits from event_template, and is used to represent 
 * physics events structured for graph neural network inference and processing.
 * 
 * @class gnn_event
 * @brief Represents a physics event for GNN inference.
 * 
 * This class provides a container for event-level observables (MET, phi, jet/lepton multiplicities),
 * MVA predictions (top quark multiplicities, signal scores, edge scores), and stores both
 * truth and reconstructed particles (tops, Z', and general GNN particles).
 * 
 * Key Features:
 * - Built-in templated reductions for extracting element properties into standard containers.
 * - `build`: Constructs the event from raw element data.
 * - `CompileEvent`: Finalizes the event structure by establishing edges and parent-child relationships.
 */
